  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale\n   - Central Idea: Utilize a hybrid global-local optimization strategy targeting a trade-off between diversity and exploitation.\n   - Bottleneck: Current method (SLSQP with softmax annealing) suffers from premature convergence. The proposed approach combines multi-start local searches with intelligent candidate selection based on the Karush-Kuhn-Tucker (KKT) conditions and projected gradient ascent.\n   - Justification: By integrating global exploration with local refinement guided by optimality conditions, we aim to escape local optima and converge faster to the global minimum.\n\n2. Mathematical Specification\n   - Objective: Minimize $C_5 = \\max_k \\int h(x)(1-h(x+k)) dx$\n   - Constraints:\n     - $0 \\leq h[i] \\leq 1 \\forall i$\n     - $\\sum h[i] \\cdot dx = 1$\n   - Formulation: Discrete approximation via correlation convolution serves as the fitness function. The optimization employs projected gradient steps guided by the Karush-Kuhn-Tucker conditions for constraint enforcement.\n   - Algorithm Selection: Conjugate gradient and KKT-based local searches within a multi-start framework.\n\n3. Implementation Procedure:\n   - Primary Initialization:\n     1. Generate initial population with physical basis vectors (sinc, triangle, rectangular pulses)\n     2. Normalize flux via KKT-inspired descent\n   - Core Loop:\n     1. KKT-guided mutation: $w_k = (h - \\lambda h)^2 \\rightarrow \\min_c$\n     2. Conjugate gradient refinement $\\nabla h \\cdot (h - C) \\geq 0$\n     3. Adaptive truncation: Keep top $p=0.2\\%$ candidates\n   - Local Refinement:\n     1. Projected gradient: $(I-\\alpha_h(I+h_h)) \\cdot \\nabla C$\n     2. Ensure $\\lambda = \\max(0,\\min(1,\\lambda))$\n   - Termination:\n     - Time passes: return best candidate\n     - Failure checks: ensure no NaN/Inf\n\n4. Search Choices:\n   - Basis vectors:\n     1. Sinc tuning: $h(x)\\propto \\text{sinc}(4\\sigma x)$\n     2. Debaised triangle pulses\n     3. Adaptive rectangle width\n   - Hyper-parameters:\n     - Gradient weight $\\alpha_h = 0.8,...,0.98$ (optimized)\n     - Mutation probability $p_m = \\min(0.3, t/t_max)$\n\n5. Budget Estimate:\n   - Core phases: 2 multi-start phases, 3 optimization steps\n   - Dominant cost: KKT projection: $O(n)$ per candidate\n   - Estimated runtime: 1200s for $n=300$, achieving 0.381 improvement\n\n6. Validation:\n   - Post-hoc checks:\n     1. $\\sum h[i] \\cdot dx = 1$\n     2. Convexity enforcement via spectral check\n   - Input/output: NumPy array $h$ with length preserved",
